1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,000
.

2
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:44,080
Absolutely keep them.

3
00:00:44,080 --> 00:00:46,480
Good morning, everyone.

4
00:00:46,480 --> 00:00:48,160
I thought the bumper video would be longer than that,

5
00:00:48,160 --> 00:00:50,760
so I appreciate you being patient with me.

6
00:00:50,760 --> 00:00:56,840
Just real quick, I want to talk about something real quick

7
00:00:56,840 --> 00:00:58,280
that God placed on my heart

8
00:00:58,280 --> 00:01:00,140
while we were listening to Hosanna there.

9
00:01:00,140 --> 00:01:03,220
As a refresher, I love Palm Sunday.

10
00:01:03,220 --> 00:01:06,820
Hosanna's not in our usual vocabulary,

11
00:01:06,820 --> 00:01:10,220
but the idea is that God save us,

12
00:01:10,220 --> 00:01:12,780
God deliver us, God protect us,

13
00:01:12,780 --> 00:01:15,400
and just so happens that's what we're talking about today.

14
00:01:15,400 --> 00:01:18,500
I'm getting a little bit of reverb there, Danny,

15
00:01:18,500 --> 00:01:20,120
but well, good morning, everyone.

16
00:01:20,120 --> 00:01:21,720
For those of you that don't know me,

17
00:01:21,720 --> 00:01:23,120
my name is Corey Smith,

18
00:01:23,120 --> 00:01:25,460
and I have the privilege,

19
00:01:25,460 --> 00:01:27,080
I don't know if you have the privilege,

20
00:01:27,080 --> 00:01:29,940
I have the privilege of being part of the teaching team

21
00:01:29,940 --> 00:01:31,060
here at Canvas Community Church.

22
00:01:31,060 --> 00:01:33,600
So welcome to Family Sunday.

23
00:01:33,600 --> 00:01:36,040
If you're visiting with us today,

24
00:01:36,040 --> 00:01:37,480
not super excited, but that's okay.

25
00:01:37,480 --> 00:01:39,640
If you're visiting with us today,

26
00:01:39,640 --> 00:01:42,100
or if you haven't taken part of it yet,

27
00:01:42,100 --> 00:01:47,880
I just encourage you to embrace the chaos a little bit.

28
00:01:47,880 --> 00:01:55,480
We use the fifth Sunday of every calendar year to kind of get together.

29
00:01:55,480 --> 00:01:57,360
Caroline talked about this a little bit,

30
00:01:57,360 --> 00:02:03,120
to get together as a church and really just embody this idea that we're in this together.

31
00:02:03,120 --> 00:02:04,540
So I'm encouraged.

32
00:02:04,540 --> 00:02:05,120
I'm excited.

33
00:02:05,120 --> 00:02:08,760
Kids, hopefully you got some coloring sheets and some cool stuff.

34
00:02:08,800 --> 00:02:10,720
If I get boring, to keep you entertained.

35
00:02:10,720 --> 00:02:13,000
So we get to do this thing.

36
00:02:13,000 --> 00:02:15,800
So before we step into Ephesians 6,

37
00:02:15,800 --> 00:02:19,920
I want to give an opportunity for everyone to kind of remember where we're at

38
00:02:19,920 --> 00:02:21,260
and what we've been talking about.

39
00:02:23,260 --> 00:02:31,100
This letter that Paul is historically given credit for is sent to Ephesus

40
00:02:31,100 --> 00:02:32,760
and is sent to the church at Ephesus.

41
00:02:32,760 --> 00:02:34,300
But Ephesus is a port city.

42
00:02:34,300 --> 00:02:39,180
And this idea that this letter of Paul was circulated around Asia Minor

43
00:02:39,180 --> 00:02:43,500
addresses what God has done in Christ to create a new people.

44
00:02:43,500 --> 00:02:47,320
Paul has told us that God blesses us in Christ,

45
00:02:47,320 --> 00:02:49,520
raised us with Christ,

46
00:02:49,520 --> 00:02:52,700
and seated us with Christ in heavenly places.

47
00:02:53,260 --> 00:02:57,700
He's told us that Jesus has broken down the dividing wall of hostility

48
00:02:57,700 --> 00:03:01,680
and made one new humanity in himself.

49
00:03:01,680 --> 00:03:06,580
He's told us that the church is the place where the manifold wisdom of God

50
00:03:06,580 --> 00:03:09,520
is made known to the rest of creation.

51
00:03:09,520 --> 00:03:13,900
He's told us that the church is a place that is being built together

52
00:03:13,900 --> 00:03:15,860
as a dwelling place for God.

53
00:03:15,860 --> 00:03:18,320
So when we come to Ephesians 6,

54
00:03:18,320 --> 00:03:22,140
I want us to keep this idea in mind as this overarching narrative.

55
00:03:23,140 --> 00:03:29,140
Because I think sometimes we think Ephesians 6, 10 through 20

56
00:03:29,140 --> 00:03:31,460
is a standalone battle message.

57
00:03:31,460 --> 00:03:34,460
And I'm going to argue that a little bit today.

58
00:03:34,460 --> 00:03:36,740
But Paul, I don't think, is changing the subject.

59
00:03:36,740 --> 00:03:39,400
He's not dropping this idea at the end of the book.

60
00:03:39,400 --> 00:03:42,380
He's bringing the point to its practical edge.

61
00:03:42,380 --> 00:03:45,440
And he's showing us what it looks like to be one people of God,

62
00:03:45,440 --> 00:03:46,880
a new creation people,

63
00:03:46,880 --> 00:03:50,880
to remain faithful in a world where our unity will be pressured,

64
00:03:50,880 --> 00:03:54,100
where our identity will be challenged,

65
00:03:54,100 --> 00:03:57,120
and where our witness will be opposed.

66
00:03:58,060 --> 00:03:59,540
So in other words, again,

67
00:03:59,540 --> 00:04:03,420
I don't think Ephesians 6 is a random battle sermon dropped at the end of Ephesians.

68
00:04:03,420 --> 00:04:07,880
It's Paul protecting what he spent the entire book arguing for.

69
00:04:08,880 --> 00:04:09,800
So if you're able,

70
00:04:09,800 --> 00:04:14,540
let's all stand for the reading of Ephesians 6, 10 through 20.

71
00:04:14,540 --> 00:04:18,340
It'll be up there on the screen.

72
00:04:18,340 --> 00:04:20,020
And I've got to get there in my Bible.

73
00:04:22,440 --> 00:04:24,020
I meant to prep this and I didn't do it,

74
00:04:24,020 --> 00:04:26,480
so we'll spend some extra time.

75
00:04:26,480 --> 00:04:29,640
Y'all used to do sword drills as kids?

76
00:04:29,640 --> 00:04:31,200
Was that part of Sunday school?

77
00:04:31,200 --> 00:04:35,600
This Bible's not the best for sword drills

78
00:04:35,600 --> 00:04:37,180
because it's very thin pages.

79
00:04:37,180 --> 00:04:39,260
All right.

80
00:04:39,260 --> 00:04:41,420
Ephesians 6, 10 through 20.

81
00:04:41,420 --> 00:04:46,240
A final word.

82
00:04:46,240 --> 00:04:50,360
Be strong in the Lord and in his mighty power.

83
00:04:51,220 --> 00:04:52,800
Put on all of God's armor

84
00:04:52,800 --> 00:04:54,560
so that you will be able to stand firm

85
00:04:54,560 --> 00:04:56,320
against all the strategies of the devil.

86
00:04:56,320 --> 00:05:00,720
For we are not fighting against flesh and blood enemies,

87
00:05:00,720 --> 00:05:05,300
but against evil rulers and authorities of the unseen world,

88
00:05:05,300 --> 00:05:07,940
against mighty powers in this dark world,

89
00:05:07,940 --> 00:05:10,040
and against evil spirits in the heavenly places.

90
00:05:10,040 --> 00:05:13,780
Therefore, put on every piece of God's armor

91
00:05:13,780 --> 00:05:17,800
so that you will be able to resist the enemy in the time of evil.

92
00:05:17,800 --> 00:05:20,140
Then, after the battle,

93
00:05:20,140 --> 00:05:22,580
you will still be standing firm.

94
00:05:22,580 --> 00:05:24,900
Stand your ground,

95
00:05:24,900 --> 00:05:26,400
putting on the belt of truth

96
00:05:26,400 --> 00:05:28,820
and the body armor of God's righteousness for shoes.

97
00:05:28,820 --> 00:05:31,020
Put on the piece that comes from the good news

98
00:05:31,020 --> 00:05:32,560
so that you will be fully prepared.

99
00:05:32,560 --> 00:05:34,220
In addition to all these,

100
00:05:34,220 --> 00:05:35,540
hold up the shield of faith

101
00:05:35,540 --> 00:05:37,420
to stop the fiery arrows of the devil.

102
00:05:37,420 --> 00:05:39,840
Put on salvation as your helmet

103
00:05:39,840 --> 00:05:41,300
and take the sword of the spirit,

104
00:05:41,300 --> 00:05:42,340
which is the word of God.

105
00:05:43,320 --> 00:05:45,580
Pray in the spirit at all times

106
00:05:45,580 --> 00:05:46,620
and on every occasion,

107
00:05:46,620 --> 00:05:49,100
stay alert and be persistent in your prayers

108
00:05:49,100 --> 00:05:50,760
for all believers everywhere.

109
00:05:50,760 --> 00:05:52,580
And pray for me too.

110
00:05:52,580 --> 00:05:54,640
Ask God to give me the right word

111
00:05:54,640 --> 00:05:58,160
so I can boldly explain God's mysterious plan

112
00:05:58,160 --> 00:06:01,000
that the good news is for Jews and Gentiles alike.

113
00:06:01,660 --> 00:06:04,460
I am in chains now still preaching this message

114
00:06:04,460 --> 00:06:05,980
as I am God's ambassador.

115
00:06:05,980 --> 00:06:08,940
So pray that I will keep on speaking boldly for him

116
00:06:08,940 --> 00:06:09,720
as I should.

117
00:06:09,720 --> 00:06:11,060
This is the word of the Lord.

118
00:06:11,060 --> 00:06:11,660
You can be seated.

119
00:06:11,660 --> 00:06:22,080
So from the beginning,

120
00:06:22,080 --> 00:06:24,780
I want to say this message

121
00:06:24,780 --> 00:06:26,440
I think is going to sound countercultural.

122
00:06:26,440 --> 00:06:27,620
And what I mean by that is

123
00:06:27,620 --> 00:06:30,080
I don't think this is going to be the kind of message

124
00:06:30,080 --> 00:06:31,600
you hear in your current news station

125
00:06:31,600 --> 00:06:33,680
or on the radio.

126
00:06:33,680 --> 00:06:34,760
Maybe on podcast.

127
00:06:34,760 --> 00:06:37,100
I'm a podcast guy.

128
00:06:37,100 --> 00:06:39,800
And the reason for that is

129
00:06:39,800 --> 00:06:41,320
because I think the powers and principalities

130
00:06:41,320 --> 00:06:42,720
that Paul is speaking about

131
00:06:42,720 --> 00:06:45,280
are always going to draw our attention away

132
00:06:45,280 --> 00:06:46,300
from the worship of God

133
00:06:46,300 --> 00:06:47,640
and the victory of Christ.

134
00:06:47,640 --> 00:06:49,600
And I think that's the reminder

135
00:06:49,600 --> 00:06:51,360
that the apostle Paul wants us to remember

136
00:06:51,360 --> 00:06:54,160
is that he wants us to stand firm.

137
00:06:54,160 --> 00:06:54,960
Why?

138
00:06:54,960 --> 00:06:57,500
Because Jesus has already won the victory.

139
00:06:57,500 --> 00:07:00,820
So children, teenagers, parents, grandparents,

140
00:07:00,820 --> 00:07:02,300
I want all of us to hear

141
00:07:02,300 --> 00:07:04,020
what God has for us this morning

142
00:07:04,020 --> 00:07:05,600
because I believe the word of God

143
00:07:05,600 --> 00:07:07,000
speaks to every age.

144
00:07:07,000 --> 00:07:09,220
Paul says in verse 13,

145
00:07:09,720 --> 00:07:11,420
pick up the full armor of God

146
00:07:11,420 --> 00:07:13,940
so that you can stand your ground.

147
00:07:13,940 --> 00:07:17,700
That's one of the most important ideas

148
00:07:17,700 --> 00:07:19,040
of this whole passage.

149
00:07:19,040 --> 00:07:23,000
So Paul is not picturing the church

150
00:07:23,000 --> 00:07:24,620
attacking anything at all.

151
00:07:24,620 --> 00:07:27,380
He's picturing the church being attacked

152
00:07:27,380 --> 00:07:28,900
by spiritual forces

153
00:07:28,900 --> 00:07:31,880
and given what it needs by Christ

154
00:07:31,880 --> 00:07:33,400
to withstand those attacks.

155
00:07:34,480 --> 00:07:36,220
See, the dominant verb in this passage

156
00:07:36,220 --> 00:07:38,900
is not attack, but stand.

157
00:07:38,900 --> 00:07:40,720
Stand against.

158
00:07:40,720 --> 00:07:43,160
Withstand in the evil day

159
00:07:43,160 --> 00:07:46,220
and having done everything, stand.

160
00:07:46,220 --> 00:07:48,620
So that matters

161
00:07:48,620 --> 00:07:50,320
because I don't want to get

162
00:07:50,320 --> 00:07:52,120
into this preconceived notion

163
00:07:52,120 --> 00:07:53,620
that the Christian life is sleepy

164
00:07:53,620 --> 00:07:54,920
or passive or easy,

165
00:07:54,920 --> 00:07:55,800
especially while we have

166
00:07:55,800 --> 00:07:58,380
our next generation in the room.

167
00:07:59,880 --> 00:08:01,460
But it is full of grace.

168
00:08:01,460 --> 00:08:03,420
It's full of peace

169
00:08:03,420 --> 00:08:05,320
and joy.

170
00:08:05,320 --> 00:08:08,400
But it's also very full

171
00:08:08,400 --> 00:08:10,160
of real spiritual conflict.

172
00:08:10,160 --> 00:08:12,960
Again, I want to reiterate this

173
00:08:12,960 --> 00:08:14,100
like the Apostle Paul,

174
00:08:14,100 --> 00:08:16,020
not conflict against people,

175
00:08:16,020 --> 00:08:18,520
not conflict against flesh and blood,

176
00:08:18,520 --> 00:08:20,140
not conflict where

177
00:08:20,140 --> 00:08:21,400
we look at our neighbor

178
00:08:21,400 --> 00:08:22,400
and decide that they're

179
00:08:22,400 --> 00:08:24,140
less than human or the enemy.

180
00:08:25,340 --> 00:08:26,580
When Paul says

181
00:08:26,580 --> 00:08:27,840
the struggle is spiritual,

182
00:08:27,840 --> 00:08:29,880
I don't think he means

183
00:08:29,880 --> 00:08:31,500
unreal or disconnected

184
00:08:31,500 --> 00:08:32,560
from everyday life.

185
00:08:32,560 --> 00:08:33,720
And I want us to get that

186
00:08:33,720 --> 00:08:35,940
because I think that matters

187
00:08:35,940 --> 00:08:37,240
in a church like ours

188
00:08:37,240 --> 00:08:38,840
where we confess to follow Jesus,

189
00:08:38,840 --> 00:08:40,500
the Prince of Peace.

190
00:08:40,500 --> 00:08:43,000
We do not believe

191
00:08:43,000 --> 00:08:44,420
the church overcomes evil

192
00:08:44,420 --> 00:08:45,960
by becoming more violent,

193
00:08:45,960 --> 00:08:46,800
more hostile,

194
00:08:46,800 --> 00:08:49,160
or more worldly in its methods.

195
00:08:49,160 --> 00:08:51,680
No, I think Paul's emphasis here

196
00:08:51,680 --> 00:08:52,720
is not militancy.

197
00:08:53,020 --> 00:08:54,160
It is resistance.

198
00:08:54,160 --> 00:08:55,740
It is resisting.

199
00:08:55,740 --> 00:08:57,820
It is remaining faithful

200
00:08:57,820 --> 00:08:58,980
under pressure.

201
00:08:58,980 --> 00:09:01,120
It is withstanding evil

202
00:09:01,120 --> 00:09:03,580
without becoming shaped by it.

203
00:09:03,580 --> 00:09:06,240
And I think I've heard

204
00:09:06,240 --> 00:09:07,660
this passage as often,

205
00:09:07,660 --> 00:09:09,420
and to the credit

206
00:09:09,420 --> 00:09:10,100
of those preachers,

207
00:09:10,100 --> 00:09:11,540
I think they meant it

208
00:09:11,540 --> 00:09:12,340
in a positive way.

209
00:09:12,340 --> 00:09:13,440
But I've also been heard

210
00:09:13,440 --> 00:09:15,320
this passage in a militant tone

211
00:09:15,320 --> 00:09:16,680
as though Paul were calling

212
00:09:16,680 --> 00:09:18,540
the church to be more aggressive,

213
00:09:18,540 --> 00:09:20,260
combatant, and triumphalist.

214
00:09:21,520 --> 00:09:22,720
But in my reading,

215
00:09:22,720 --> 00:09:25,420
I see Paul saying stand.

216
00:09:25,420 --> 00:09:26,800
Resist.

217
00:09:26,800 --> 00:09:29,100
Having done everything, stand.

218
00:09:29,100 --> 00:09:31,820
So I don't think this is a call

219
00:09:31,820 --> 00:09:32,300
for the church

220
00:09:32,300 --> 00:09:34,000
to become more violent in spirit.

221
00:09:34,000 --> 00:09:36,060
This is a call for the church

222
00:09:36,060 --> 00:09:38,660
to become more steadfast in Christ

223
00:09:38,660 --> 00:09:40,400
in the victory that he has won.

224
00:09:40,400 --> 00:09:43,180
Because our struggle

225
00:09:43,180 --> 00:09:44,620
is not against flesh and blood.

226
00:09:44,620 --> 00:09:46,760
The church must remember something.

227
00:09:47,700 --> 00:09:49,680
Children, you must learn this early.

228
00:09:49,680 --> 00:09:50,740
And adults,

229
00:09:50,740 --> 00:09:52,740
we need to remember this often.

230
00:09:52,740 --> 00:09:55,440
People are not our enemy.

231
00:09:55,440 --> 00:09:57,980
That matters in families.

232
00:09:57,980 --> 00:09:59,740
That matters in churches.

233
00:09:59,740 --> 00:10:01,860
That matters in disagreements.

234
00:10:01,860 --> 00:10:03,700
And that matters how you engage

235
00:10:03,700 --> 00:10:04,760
with the world around you.

236
00:10:04,760 --> 00:10:07,400
If Ephesians has told us anything,

237
00:10:07,400 --> 00:10:08,420
it is that Christ

238
00:10:08,420 --> 00:10:10,520
is making one new humanity

239
00:10:10,520 --> 00:10:11,800
in himself.

240
00:10:13,320 --> 00:10:14,660
So we cannot preach unity

241
00:10:14,660 --> 00:10:15,720
in chapters two and three

242
00:10:15,720 --> 00:10:17,080
and then act like flesh and blood

243
00:10:17,080 --> 00:10:17,700
is the real enemy

244
00:10:17,700 --> 00:10:18,420
in chapter six.

245
00:10:18,420 --> 00:10:19,040
We tracking?

246
00:10:19,040 --> 00:10:23,620
The real enemy

247
00:10:23,620 --> 00:10:25,460
would love for us

248
00:10:25,460 --> 00:10:26,300
to turn on one another.

249
00:10:26,300 --> 00:10:28,220
He would love

250
00:10:28,220 --> 00:10:29,480
to disciple each other

251
00:10:29,480 --> 00:10:30,180
in fear,

252
00:10:30,180 --> 00:10:31,280
suspicion,

253
00:10:31,280 --> 00:10:32,840
outrage, bitterness,

254
00:10:32,840 --> 00:10:34,160
and more division.

255
00:10:35,000 --> 00:10:36,080
He would love for us

256
00:10:36,080 --> 00:10:36,640
to forget

257
00:10:36,640 --> 00:10:38,740
that the gospel

258
00:10:38,740 --> 00:10:39,340
forms us

259
00:10:39,340 --> 00:10:40,640
into a new kind

260
00:10:40,640 --> 00:10:41,180
of people,

261
00:10:41,180 --> 00:10:43,340
a peaceable people,

262
00:10:43,340 --> 00:10:45,080
a truthful people,

263
00:10:45,080 --> 00:10:46,540
a faithful people,

264
00:10:46,540 --> 00:10:48,360
people who know

265
00:10:48,360 --> 00:10:50,220
how to withstand.

266
00:10:50,220 --> 00:10:52,340
And not on our own merit,

267
00:10:52,340 --> 00:10:54,260
but because we believe

268
00:10:54,260 --> 00:10:55,180
in the victory

269
00:10:55,180 --> 00:10:56,100
that Christ has won.

270
00:10:56,100 --> 00:10:57,640
And I've got a slot up here.

271
00:10:57,640 --> 00:10:58,980
I don't think

272
00:10:58,980 --> 00:11:00,620
the gospel teaches us

273
00:11:00,620 --> 00:11:02,620
to how to conquer the world.

274
00:11:03,620 --> 00:11:04,840
The gospel teaches us

275
00:11:04,840 --> 00:11:05,820
how to stand

276
00:11:05,820 --> 00:11:07,080
in the victory of Jesus

277
00:11:07,080 --> 00:11:08,340
because he's already done it.

278
00:11:08,340 --> 00:11:10,020
Tracking?

279
00:11:10,020 --> 00:11:12,820
Before Paul tells the church

280
00:11:12,820 --> 00:11:14,180
to put on the armor of God,

281
00:11:14,180 --> 00:11:15,820
I've got some friends

